# Testing

## Test Pyramid

| Layer | Pattern | DB | Runner |
|-------|---------|-----|--------|
| Unit | `*.spec.ts` | Mocked | Parallel |
| Integration | `*.integration.spec.ts` | Real (Testcontainers) | `--runInBand` |
| E2E | `*.e2e-spec.ts` | Real (Testcontainers) | `--runInBand` |

## Testcontainers

- `test/setup/global-setup.ts` starts ONE `PostgreSqlContainer`, pushes schema, writes URL to `/tmp/.test-db-url`
- `test/helpers/prisma-test.helper.ts` provides singleton PrismaClient with `clean()` (TRUNCATE all tables)

## Factories

```typescript
class UserFactory {
  build(overrides?)       // returns plain object (no DB)
  create(overrides?)      // persists to DB
  createMany(count, overrides?)
}
```

Factories auto-create required relations (e.g., `PostFactory` creates a `User` unless `userId` is overridden).

## Rules

- Every `beforeEach` in integration/e2e calls `db.clean()`
- Use factories for ALL test data — never hardcode objects inline
- Descriptive names: `it('should throw ConflictException when email is already taken')`
- Always test happy path AND error path for every service method
- Assert the negative: `expect(result).not.toHaveProperty('password')`
- Integration tests verify DB state directly after operations
- E2E tests verify status codes, response body shape, field values, and absence of sensitive fields

## Mocking (Unit Tests Only)

- `createMockPrismaService()` returns `jest.fn()` for every method used
- Never mock in integration or E2E tests
- `jest.clearAllMocks()` in `afterEach`
